"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[1050],{438:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"new","desc":"","params":[{"name":"settings","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"deps","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":79,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"enqueue","desc":"Writes a ticket and its lane index, rolling back on any failure so a partial\\nenqueue never leaves a user reserved against a ticket that does not exist.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"request","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":230,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_claimTicket","desc":"Moves one ticket from `Queued` to `Claimed`, repairing stale claims on the\\nway.\\n\\nA claim past its deadline means its owner stopped. What it left behind\\ndepends on how far it got: if the referenced match reached `Ready`, the\\nplayers are genuinely matched, so the ticket is finalized under that match\\nrather than stolen. If the match is still `Claiming` past its own deadline it\\nnever committed, so it is marked `Aborted` and the ticket is taken.\\n\\nTickets whose origin server has stopped heartbeating are refused, since a\\nmatch containing them could not be delivered.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"candidate","desc":"","lua_type":"Candidate"},{"name":"matchId","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"owned","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"any?\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":620,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_commit","desc":"Turns a group of candidates into a committed match, or into nothing.\\n\\nThe order of these steps is load-bearing:\\n\\n1. **Sort the ticket ids.** Two workers contending for overlapping tickets\\n   acquire them in the same order and so cannot deadlock.\\n2. **Write the `Claiming` record.** A crash after this leaves a record\\n   another worker can resolve, rather than claims pointing at nothing.\\n3. **Claim every ticket.** Any refusal aborts and returns the rest to\\n   `Queued`. No hook has run yet, so nothing needs compensating.\\n4. **Validate the lease** before doing anything expensive.\\n5. **Run `finalize`.** The only step that yields and the only one with side\\n   effects outside Muster. The lease is renewed first so a slow hook cannot\\n   outlive it, the return value is validated and size-checked, and the lease\\n   is validated **again** afterwards because time passed.\\n6. **Compare-and-set `Claiming` to `Ready`.** Guarded on server id, lease\\n   epoch and deadline together, so a worker that lost its lease cannot commit\\n   even if it reaches this line. This is the linearization point: before it\\n   the match does not exist, after it it does.\\n7. **Then** mark tickets matched, unlock parties, and announce.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"group","desc":"","lua_type":"{ Candidate }"},{"name":"owned","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"boolean\\n"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":728,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"_deliver","desc":"Delivers a committed match to this server, if it holds any of the players.\\n\\nDeduplicated on matchId, so a match arriving by commit, by announcement and\\nby poll fires the signal once.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"envelope","desc":"","lua_type":"any"},{"name":"source","desc":"","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"dedupe","desc":"","lua_type":"boolean"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":937,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"step","desc":"One pass: upkeep on local tickets, lane acquisition, then a scan of each held\\nlane.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1044,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"start","desc":"","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1057,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}},{"name":"stop","desc":"Stops the loop and releases every lease this server holds, so another server\\ncan take the lanes immediately rather than after the 15-second timeout.","params":[{"name":"self","desc":"","lua_type":"any"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":1084,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"Engine","desc":"The coordination layer behind [Matchmaker].\\n\\nEvery server runs the same loop and acts as both producer and worker; there\\nis no dedicated matchmaker server.\\n\\n### The loop\\n\\n1. **Enqueue.** Reserve each member\'s userId by compare-and-set so a player\\n   cannot hold two tickets, write the ticket, then write a denormalized copy\\n   into the lane\'s sorted map, keyed by queue time.\\n2. **Acquire.** Take leases on the lanes this server\'s own tickets landed in.\\n   The lease holder does the matching for that lane.\\n3. **Scan.** Read the oldest candidates and run [Matcher] over them.\\n4. **Commit.** Two-phase and fenced; see `_commit`.\\n5. **Deliver.** Announce the match to the servers holding its players. Those\\n   servers also poll, so delivery does not depend on the announcement.\\n\\n### Recovery\\n\\nState is recovered by expiry rather than cleanup:\\n\\n| Failure | Recovery |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Worker dies holding a lease | The lease expires after 15 s and the next holder takes it at a higher epoch, which rejects any late write from the dead one |\\n| Worker dies mid-commit | Claims expire; the next worker adopts the match if it committed, and aborts it if it did not |\\n| Producer dies with tickets queued | Heartbeats stop and the tickets expire within `ticketExpiration` |","source":{"line":33,"path":"src/internal/Engine.luau"}}')}}]);